🚽 Test case: #196 -- same as struct_field_brace_init_tag_mismatch_fail
🚽 but for a non-struct element (`{&n}` for a plain `rizz n`), the
🚽 category-mismatch sub-case of PR #248 review round 5, finding 1 --
🚽 infer_expression_struct_name() reports an empty tag for a
🚽 confirmed-non-struct expression the same as for a genuinely unknown
🚽 one, so the category check (VarType/pointer_level) has to run first
🚽 and independently, same as the round-3/round-4 fixes for other storage
🚽 sites.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};
gang Holder {
    gang Point *pt;
};

skibidi bump(gang Point *pp) {
    yapping("%d", pp.x);
}

skibidi main {
    rizz n;
    n = 42;
    gang Holder h = { &n };
    bump(h.pt);
}
